**Failure Handling Model**

A realistic production-ready architecture should define failure boundaries:

```text
If APIM blocks request
-> user gets controlled 429 or policy-driven error

If Function validation fails
-> user gets clean 400 with friendly UI message

If Function cannot get token
-> backend logs auth failure, user gets generic service error

If Foundry times out
-> Function returns graceful fallback message
   such as "I’m having trouble right now, please try again."

If Foundry returns malformed or unexpected output
-> Function normalizes or suppresses unsafe/internal fields
```

This matters because a chat experience must fail politely. Raw backend failures should never leak into the UI.

